k of the large, historic dining room. It was like we had been transported back in time to the 1930s. It was so classy and beautiful with all of the tables in the room with the wood ceiling. All I know is that both of my parents would have absolutely loved this dining room. I felt like they were both there with me during the meal..."},{"business_id":"24f-qQokEN2UvBNHMWLm3A","review_id":"pRac_bHGAd6B1hgfC0mGSA","date":"2017-12-23T04:34:55","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9514355659484863,"text_excerpt":"Ok WOW. this place is definitely a restaurant that I'll remember forever. My friend and I decided to go super last minute, so we didn't make a reservation. Got dressed up (definitely a coat & tie/ nice top & heels kind of place), and got super lucky and was given the last table. We got the Rockefeller oysters to start, which were surprisingly really good! They're the original place to serve them, and with New Orleans being known for their oysters, this was definitely a must try. They serve them hot, on a plate of hot salt rock! Surprised us since they're usually on ice. For our main course I got the soft shell crab amandine and I wish I could tell you what kind of fish my friend got.. eit..."},{"business_id":"24f-qQokEN2UvBNHMWLm3A","review_id":"KuDwpSvKsIxczOJ1MSqVZg","date":"2017-12-02T16:47:29","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9461001753807068,"text_excerpt":"Antoine's is one of the oldest restaurants in New Orleans still run by the original family and that is pretty cool and what makes New Orleans so rich in history. As a local, I could not pass up the 2017 fall lunch special which was 3 courses for $20.17. (read: if its still 2017 when you read this book a lunch ASAP). They do a similar lunch special in the summer so check their website to stay on top of their specials. On top of the 3 courses for $20.17 you can also take full advantage of their 25 cent cocktails which changes daily. The moment we sat down our server greeted us and asked if we had ever 